Z||000001||sqoach||11-05-2001||01:31 PM||||Well, there's always that chrome paint. $3-$4 a can. Can't get any cheaper than that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||fix||11-05-2001||03:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B>Well, there's always that chrome paint. $3-$4 a can. Can't get any cheaper than that   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Stay away from the chrome spray paint.  That stuff is worthless in my opinion.  I'm not sure what your alternatives are, but use the chrome spray paint only as a last resort.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||11-05-2001||03:42 PM||||all those 'chrome/silver' paints look fine until you touch them. Try going to hardware store and find some chrome or stainless tubing you can push down over the original.||||reg||1
Z||000004||sqoach||11-05-2001||04:10 PM||||I was kidding about the paint. That stuff does suck. I'm not sure why it doesn't set like regular paint. One of my friends younger brother painted his wheels with that stuff. And well...it looked good from about 50 feet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
